From: Kettle Linux
Subject: [PATCH] sensor: log a failed request before handing its error on

sensor_open_ready() and sensor_close_ready() give the GError to the
task, drop their task reference (completing it frees the error), and
then print error->message: a use-after-free. Any failed enable or
disable request crashes the client in g_log(). It shows after an ADSP
restart, when the next enable goes to the Sensor Core that went away:
kettle-motiond segfaulted in vasprintf under g_log from
sensor_open_ready. Log first.
---
diff --git a/src/libssc-sensor.c b/src/libssc-sensor.c
index 59d587b..70e879e 100644
--- a/src/libssc-sensor.c
+++ b/src/libssc-sensor.c
@@ -106,9 +106,9 @@ sensor_close_ready (SSCClient *self, GAsyncResult *result, gpointer user_data)
 	GError *error = NULL;
 
 	if (!ssc_client_send_finish (self, result, &error)) {
+		g_debug ("Sensor disable request failed: %s", error->message);
 		g_task_return_error (task, error);
 		g_clear_object (&task);
-		g_debug ("Sensor disable request failed: %s", error->message);
 		return;
 	}
 
@@ -168,9 +168,9 @@ sensor_open_ready (SSCClient *self, GAsyncResult *result, gpointer user_data)
 	GError *error = NULL;
 
 	if (!ssc_client_send_finish (self, result, &error)) {
+		g_debug ("Sensor enable request failed: %s", error->message);
 		g_task_return_error (task, error);
 		g_clear_object (&task);
-		g_debug ("Sensor enable request failed: %s", error->message);
 		return;
 	}
 
